            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0519" n="507" xml:id="pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/5118</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Valencia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-24">April 24, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 35 of March 15, 1937, regarding American deserters from the Spanish
                    Army.</p>
                <p>The Department has noted with interest the contents of your despatch and
                    particularly your estimate that there are approximately 1,700 American citizens
                    serving in the Spanish Government forces in Spain. The Department desires to be
                    informed whether your estimate includes persons of dual nationality who were
                    residing in Spain at the outbreak of the civil war or whether it includes only
                    Americans who have gone to Spain since that time.</p>
                <p>With reference to the last paragraph of your despatch, it is requested that you
                    forward to the Department the uniform of the deserter R … which is said to have
                    been issued to him in New York before he left this country.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur
                            J. Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
